# Data files keep LF line endings on every platform.
#
# Git for Windows converts LF to CRLF on checkout by default. A TSV read back
# with CRLF endings gets a trailing \r on its last column's header, so a
# lookup by that name finds nothing. That once turned the unindexed-foreign-
# key column into a table of zeros. The scripts now split on \r?\n, but the
# files should not change underneath them in the first place.
*.tsv  text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.mjs  text eol=lf
